COMMA OPERATOR ( , ):
- This operator has least priority according to the associativity.
- Comma operator can also used in both brackets and without brackets.
- If we are using comma inside brackets (,) - it performs as an operator.
- Without brackets ',' it performs as a seperator.
- In operator it considers only the right most variable/element in the function/condition. (last one)
- In seperator it considers the left most variable/element in the function/condition. (first one)

eg:
seperator:
a = 10, 20, 30
output:
a = 10

operator:
b = (10, 20, 30)
output:
b = 30

eg:
x=1, y=1
int a, b;
a = x++, ++x, x--;
b = (y++, ++y, y--);
printf("%d %d %d %d", a, b, x, y);
output:
a = 1, b = 3, x = 2, y = 2

eg:
a = 10, b = 0, c = -1;
if(a, c, b)
printf("True");
else
printf("False");

output:
