TERNARY OPERATOR: (? :)
- It is similar to if-else condition.

eg:
check whether the number is odd or even

num%2==0? printf("Even") : printf("Odd');
- here ? acts as if
- and : acts as else

eg:
check which number is largest

n1> n2? printf("n1 is largest") : printf("n2 is largest");

eg:
check which is highest in given 3 integers
- nested if

n1 > n2 ? n1 > n3? printf("n1 is largest") : printf("n3 is largest") : n2 > n3? printf("n2 is largest") : printf("n3 is largest");

- first grouping will happen, associativity for operators is "right - to - left"
- so the conditions are checked according to the associativity and generates the output.
- inside ternary operator we cannot use keywords(like break , continue, int, etc)
